-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Acknowledgments
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These scripts are designed to run within PixInsight (https://pixinsight.com/), a commercial image
processing platform developed by Pleiades Astrophoto S.L. This product is based on software
from the PixInsight project, developed by Pleiades Astrophoto and its contributors
(https://pixinsight.com/).

Part 1 — Lazy Workflow Part 1

Plate solving uses PixInsight's own ImageSolver script, (C) 2012-2024 Andrés del Pozo /
(C) 2019-2024 Juan Conejero (PTeam), including its blind solver for images without coordinates.
Part 1 includes ImageSolver from the PixInsight installation; it is not distributed with this
software. No external programs are launched.

Standard PixInsight processes called by this script: SpectroPhotometricFluxCalibration,
MultiscaleGradientCorrection, GradientCorrection, and DynamicBackgroundExtraction.

Part 2 — Lazy Workflow Part 2

Auto Display Stretch (linked/unlinked) sets PixInsight's ScreenTransferFunction with the AutoSTF
method by Juan Conejero / Pleiades Astrophoto; the script adds the automatic linked/unlinked choice
and sky statistics from the background preview.

Background finder concept inspired by FindBackground by Gerrit Erdt and Franklin Marek
(SetiAstro), licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0 (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/). Our
implementation is independently written with a different algorithm and scoring approach.

Standard PixInsight processes called by this script: SpectrophotometricColorCalibration (SPCC),
BackgroundNeutralization, ColorCalibration.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Files, Programs and Internet Access
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- External programs: none. Both scripts run entirely inside PixInsight.
- Internet, Part 1: only through PixInsight's ImageSolver. If the local Gaia star catalogue is not
  installed (or for limit magnitudes of 5 or less), ImageSolver downloads catalogue stars from the
  VizieR service set in its preferences, sending the image's centre coordinates and search radius.
- Internet, Part 2: only when "Check dust map" is clicked in the background pre-check. The image's
  centre coordinates and field size are sent over https to the NASA/IPAC IRSA Galactic Dust
  Reddening and Extinction service (https://irsa.ipac.caltech.edu/applications/DUST/); the dust
  map (SFD map, Schlegel, Finkbeiner & Davis 1998) is downloaded to the system temporary folder
  and deleted afterwards.
- Files outside the PixInsight installation: settings are kept in PixInsight's own settings.
  ImageSolver writes star lists (stars*.csv) to the system temporary folder. Part 1 searches the
  PixInsight folders, common Astro folders and a folder the user picks for the MARS database
  (.xmars, read only), and reads/writes separation profiles (.txt) only in a folder the user
  chooses. Re-run marks are stored as XISF properties in the image; Part 1 adds FITS HISTORY lines
  starting with "SH:" when a gradient model is applied.

Details: "Files, Programs and Internet Access" in the user guides of Part 1 and Part 2.

